for a = 10:20
 fprintf('value of a: %d\n',a);
end

a = 10;
while(a < 20)
 fprintf('value of a: %d\n',a);
 a = a + 1;
end

a = 10;
while(a < 20)
 fprintf('value of a: %d\n',a);
 a = a + 1;
 if(a > 15)
  break;
 end
end
Because printing occurs before increment and test, the last printed value is 15.

a = 9;
while a < 20
 a = a + 1;
 if a == 15
  continue;
 end
 fprintf('value of a: %d\n',a);
end
Increment occurs before continue, so 15 is skipped and the loop still makes progress. The last printed value is 20, since the prior test was made at 19.

